#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(273.12pt, 753.36pt, "Page ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(299.4pt, 753.36pt, "11")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(310.68pt, 753.36pt, " of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(326.64pt, 753.36pt, "16")
  #line-at(54pt, 83.16pt, "Discussion and Conclusions ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 111pt, "We demonstrated a fabrication method that enables the creation of three-dimensional structures directly ")
  #line-at(54pt, 124.8pt, "from liquid polymers, shaped by boundary conditions in weightlessness. The approach, which we termed ")
  #line-at(54pt, 138.6pt, "LiquiFab, extends the concept of form-finding")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(290.4pt, 134.04pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.48pt, 138.6pt, " into a practical manufacturing process. It is scale-")
  #line-at(54pt, 152.4pt, "invariant, zero-waste, and capable of producing continuous, structurally robust volumes within minutes. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 166.2pt, "It is compatible with a wide range of materials and can produce both soft and rigid objects.  ")
  #line-at(54pt, 193.92pt, "LiquiFab defines a new class of manufacturing methods, differing fundamentally from additive processes ")
  #line-at(54pt, 207.72pt, "such as fused deposition modeling (FDM)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(258.96pt, 203.16pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(263.04pt, 207.72pt, ", rapid liquid printing (RLP)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(400.8pt, 203.16pt, "15")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(408.96pt, 207.72pt, ", or stereolithography (SLA)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(546.96pt, 203.16pt, "10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(555.12pt, 207.72pt, ". ")
  #line-at(54pt, 221.52pt, "In all of these, the printing head or light pattern must effectively visit every voxel in space to define the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 235.32pt, "final geometry. These approaches provide exceptional geometric freedom but are intrinsically non-")
  #line-at(54pt, 249.12pt, "scalable in time, as printing duration grows directly with the volume of the object. A fundamentally ")
  #line-at(54pt, 262.92pt, "different strategy is introduced by volumetric additive manufacturing via tomographic reconstruction ")
  #line-at(54pt, 276.72pt, "(VAM)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(89.88pt, 272.16pt, "16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(98.04pt, 276.72pt, ", in which the entire object is formed simultaneously rather than through sequential voxel ")
  #line-at(54pt, 290.52pt, "addressing. However, VAM relies on optical penetration through the photopolymer, imposing physical ")
  #line-at(54pt, 304.32pt, "limits on object size and material choice.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(253.44pt, 299.76pt, "17")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(261.6pt, 304.32pt, " Moreover, only a fraction of the resin volume contributes to ")
  #line-at(54pt, 318.12pt, "the final solid, as the surrounding polymer is typically discarded after exposure.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(436.92pt, 313.56pt, "16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 345.96pt, "LiquiFab cannot provide the full geometric freedom offered by 3D printing methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(464.16pt, 341.4pt, "9,10,16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(488.28pt, 345.96pt, ", but within its ")
  #line-at(54pt, 359.76pt, "accessible geometric space, it provides unprecedented advantages. The formation of 3D objects is ")
  #line-at(54pt, 373.56pt, "governed solely by interfacial physics and is independent of light propagation or voxel-by-voxel motion. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 387.36pt, "This is particularly advantageous for large-scale constructions, where conventional printing would ")
  #line-at(54pt, 401.16pt, "become prohibitively slow, and where the overall form and strength of the structure take priority over fine ")
  #line-at(54pt, 414.96pt, "geometrical details. Because the formed body is fluidically continuous, it naturally yields homogenous ")
  #line-at(54pt, 428.76pt, "and smooth structures, without the characteristic layers of 3D printing.   ")
  #line-at(54pt, 456.48pt, "The practical scale of a structure fabricated under simulated weightlessness is limited by two factors: the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 470.28pt, "maximum size is bounded by the physical dimensions of the immersion liquid container, and by imperfect ")
  #line-at(54pt, 484.08pt, "density matching, which leads to a finite capillary length. In space, LiquiFab is entirely free of these ")
  #line-at(54pt, 497.88pt, "limitations, as an immersion liquid is no longer necessary. Therefore, the process is not confined to a ")
  #line-at(54pt, 511.68pt, "manufacturing envelope, and structures could, in principle, grow to any size. The combination of zero-")
  #line-at(54pt, 525.48pt, "waste operation, scale invariance, and insensitivity to gravity makes LiquiFab a promising candidate for ")
  #line-at(54pt, 539.28pt, "in-situ fabrication of large structures in space. Several studies, including Yerazunis et al")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(481.44pt, 534.72pt, "18")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(489.6pt, 539.28pt, " and Crowe et ")
  #line-at(54pt, 553.08pt, "al")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(62.64pt, 548.52pt, "19")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 553.08pt, ", have already developed space-grade formulations that can withstand deep vacuum, radiation, and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 566.88pt, "atomic oxygen, and could thus be excellent candidates for LiquiFab in space.  ")
  #line-at(54pt, 594.72pt, "Our present demonstration used a single nozzle as the end effector. With one injector, the constructed ")
  #line-at(54pt, 608.52pt, "geometry is always converging—two existing boundary conditions merge into a single new one. Future ")
  #line-at(54pt, 622.32pt, "implementations may employ dual or multiple injectors, such that each boundary could lead to two or ")
  #line-at(54pt, 636.12pt, "more new ones. This would enable the creation of diverging geometries, such as tree-like branches or ")
  #line-at(54pt, 649.92pt, "networked structures. Another useful enhancement would be to allow the injector to rotate freely on a ball ")
  #line-at(54pt, 663.72pt, "bearing, enabling injection from orientations currently inaccessible due to geometric constraints of the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 677.52pt, "robotic arm. ")
]

