  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(327pt, 753.36pt, "16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 20.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 90.72pt, "Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 121.92pt, "Materials ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 150pt, "To create a simulated zero-gravity environment, we filled a glass container with an immersion liquid ")
  #line-at(54pt, 163.8pt, "consisting of Deionized (DI) water and glycerol (Bio-Lab, Israel; Cat No. 000712050100). We tuned the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 177.6pt, "density of this solution to match the density of the specific liquid polymer under test. To ensure precise ")
  #line-at(54pt, 191.4pt, "density matching, we monitored the solution's concentration using a refractometer (ATC, USA; Range: ")
  #line-at(54pt, 205.2pt, "0–32% Brix). ")
  #line-at(54pt, 233.04pt, "We prepared two types of polymers: a single-component UV-cured resin and a two-component silicone ")
  #line-at(54pt, 246.84pt, "elastomer. Following preparation, we degassed both polymer types under a negative pressure of 0.7 to 0.8 ")
  #line-at(54pt, 260.64pt, "atm to remove trapped air bubbles.  UV-cured resin: We used Vida Rosa UV resin, optionally colored ")
  #line-at(54pt, 274.44pt, "with a translucent resin dye (Miraclekoo). We adjusted the immersion liquid for this material to a Brix ")
  #line-at(54pt, 288.24pt, "value between 25% and 27%, depending on the concentration of the colorant dye (Fig. 1j-k, Fig. 2, Fig. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 302.04pt, "3e, Fig. 4e-h, and supplementary Fig. 5a). PDMS Elastomer: As a two-component control, we utilized the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 315.84pt, "SYLGARD 184 Silicone Elastomer Kit. We adjusted the immersion liquid for the PDMS experiments to ")
  #line-at(54pt, 329.64pt, "a Brix value of 9.5 ± 0.2% (Supplementary Fig. 5b). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 359.4pt, "Experimental systems ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 387.36pt, "Basic system.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(122.28pt, 387.36pt, " Supplementary Fig. 1 presents the experimental setup used in Fig. 2. The system is based ")
  #line-at(54pt, 401.16pt, "on a 2000 ml glass (borosilicate 3.3) cylindrical container with a diameter of 13 cm. Resting on top of the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 414.96pt, "container is a ‘Fixator’ – a printed (PLA; Bambu Lab, X-1 Carbon) element that consists of a circular ring ")
  #line-at(54pt, 428.76pt, "from which multiple arms extend into the container. The arms hold the bounding surfaces, which were ")
  #line-at(54pt, 442.56pt, "full when they served only as geometrical constraints and hollow when they were also used as sources for ")
  #line-at(54pt, 456.36pt, "polymer injection. The boundaries were either printed as an integral part of the fixator or made from ")
  #line-at(54pt, 470.16pt, "molded silicon (Specialty Resin & Chemical; Cast-a-mold platinum food-grade silicone rubber, Hardness ")
  #line-at(54pt, 483.96pt, "20 shore A) when easy detachment of the final object was desired. When serving as nozzles for liquid ")
  #line-at(54pt, 497.76pt, "injection, the bounding elements were connected via silicone tubing to a syringe, which was operated ")
  #line-at(54pt, 511.56pt, "either manually or with a syringe pump (Cole-Parmer, USA; Cat No 74900-15).   ")
  #line-at(54pt, 539.16pt, "The container was placed on three poles within a 51 cm diameter plaster polymerization sphere, internally ")
  #line-at(54pt, 552.96pt, "coated with Barium Sulfate (BaSO4) powder (CS-chemicals, Israel; CAS No. 7727-43-7), such that the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 566.76pt, "3D polymer shape is roughly centered. The polymerization sphere contained three 900 mW UV 365 nm ")
  #line-at(54pt, 580.56pt, "LED sources (Luminus Devices; P/No SST-10-UV-A130-G365-00) equally spaced along its equator. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 594.36pt, "Three circular optical baffles (coated on both sides with BaSO4) with a 50 mm diameter were located 40 ")
  #line-at(54pt, 608.16pt, "mm in front of each LED. The entire setup was constructed on a 60 cm by 60 cm honeycomb breadboard ")
  #line-at(54pt, 621.96pt, "optical table (Thorlabs, USA; P/NoB6060A) to suppress vibrations.      ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 649.56pt, "Robotic System. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(139.68pt, 649.56pt, "Supplementary Fig. 2 depicts the components of the robotic system shown in Fig. 4. At ")
  #line-at(54pt, 663.36pt, "the heart of the system is a silicone nozzle that serves as both a boundary condition and the injection point ")
  #line-at(54pt, 677.16pt, "for the polymer. The nozzle was mounted on a brass elbow, which was attached on its other end to the tip ")
  #line-at(54pt, 690.96pt, "of a 22 cm hollow stainless-steel pipe. The metal pipe was secured to the endplate of a six-degree-of-")
]

// arXiv source page 15
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(272.76pt, 753.36pt, "Page ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(299.04pt, 753.36pt, "15")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(311.04pt, 753.36pt, " of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(327pt, 753.36pt, "16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 83.16pt, "freedom robotic arm (Mitsubishi, Japan; MELFA RV-6SD) using a custom 3D-printed adapter coupled ")
  #line-at(54pt, 96.96pt, "with standard mechanical fittings. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 124.8pt, "Liquid polymer was supplied to the nozzle through a silicone tube that led from a 60 cc syringe mounted ")
  #line-at(54pt, 138.6pt, "on a syringe pump (Cetoni, Germany; Nemesys), through the pipe, and into the brass elbow. Any segment ")
  #line-at(54pt, 152.4pt, "of the polymer route that could be exposed to stray light or the polymerization light was wrapped with ")
  #line-at(54pt, 166.2pt, "Kapton tape (DuPont, USA; Kapton) to prevent premature polymerization.  ")
  #line-at(54pt, 193.92pt, "The polymerization sphere was composed of a base that housed the water container and a slitted lid that ")
  #line-at(54pt, 207.72pt, "allowed the nozzle to remain submerged even when the lid was closed. During the robotic operation, the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 221.52pt, "sphere was kept open to allow free motion of the arm, and the lid was placed only during polymerization ")
  #line-at(54pt, 235.32pt, "steps. The base included a clear glass plate fixed at approximately 11 cm from the bottom. Three UV ")
  #line-at(54pt, 249.12pt, "LEDs (Luminus Devices; P/No SST-10-UV-A130-G365-00) covered with 35 mm optical baffles were ")
  #line-at(54pt, 262.92pt, "located at the bottom of the sphere such that they illuminated the volume through the glass plate. All ")
  #line-at(54pt, 276.72pt, "structural components of the sphere - the base, lid, and baffles – were 3D-printed in white PLA (Bambu ")
  #line-at(54pt, 290.52pt, "Lab X-1 Carbon) and coated internally with BaSO₄ (CS-Chemicals, Israel; CAS No 7727-43-7) to ensure ")
  #line-at(54pt, 304.32pt, "uniform diffuse reflection.  ")
  #line-at(54pt, 332.16pt, "The immersion liquid was contained in a 2000 ml borosilicate (3.3) cylindrical vessel, 19 cm in diameter, ")
  #line-at(54pt, 345.96pt, "which was affixed to the glass plate using double-sided mounting tape (Gorilla Glue Company, USA; ")
  #line-at(54pt, 359.76pt, "Gorilla Tough and Clear). ")
  #line-at(54pt, 387.48pt, "The robot was programmed with Mitsubishi’s ‘MELFA-Basic V’ programming language and operated ")
  #line-at(54pt, 401.28pt, "using its dedicated software (Mitsubishi, Japan; RT toolbox 3).  The syringe pump was operated via the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 415.08pt, "Cetoni software (Cetoni, Germany; neMESYS UserInterface v 2.6.0.4).  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 458.4pt, "3D scanning and surface comparison ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 486.48pt, "Scanning was performed using a structured light scanner (Zeiss, Germany; GOM Scan 1 (200)) with the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 500.28pt, "object placed on a rotating table (Zeiss, Germany; GOM ROT 350). The Zeiss Inspect software ")
  #line-at(54pt, 514.08pt, "automatically stitches the obtained images to produce the three-dimensional digital representation. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 527.88pt, "Because the LiquiFab objects are highly transparent, they were coated with a single layer of masking spray ")
  #line-at(54pt, 541.68pt, "(AESUB, Germany; AESUB orange) estimated by the manufacturer to have a thickness of 5-6 microns.  ")
  #line-at(54pt, 555.48pt, "Comparison between the scanned geometries and the computationally predicted ones was also performed ")
  #line-at(54pt, 569.28pt, "using the Zeiss Inspect software using the following parameters: ‘Prealignment’ - ON, ‘Compute ")
  #line-at(54pt, 583.08pt, "additional best-fit’ – ON, ‘Create Surface Comparison On CAD’ with ‘Max. Distance’ = 0.50 mm, ")
  #line-at(54pt, 596.76pt, "‘Collect local deviation peaks’ – ON, ‘Max. deviation of normal’ = 60°, ‘Max. opening angle’ = 30°. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 626.28pt, "Code availability ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 654.36pt, "The Grasshopper Surface Evolver (GSE) tool is freely available at https://github.com/Amir-")
  #line-at(54pt, 668.16pt, "Mann/surface_evolver_grasshopper/. ")
]

